{"id": "EUVD-2026-15308", "enisaUuid": "ceda771a-8581-363b-bb99-e0bf4b0d554b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\naccel/amdxdna: Fix crash when destroying a suspended hardware context\n\nIf userspace issues an ioctl to destroy a hardware context that has\nalready been automatically suspended, the driver may crash because the\nmailbox channel pointer is NULL for the suspended context.\n\nFix this by checking the mailbox channel pointer in aie2_destroy_context()\nbefore accessing it.", "datePublished": "2026-03-25T10:27:29", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T10:06:58", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2d2c32b1b9e32f25214f0cbc818c4d55f7da1d0e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a6317704edab95d66a62fc1861d9546284ab678e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8363c02863332992a1822688da41f881d88d1631"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-23341", "GHSA-g743-x9vq-5fpv"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3ac52e1c-6969-38cf-a909-38feffcfa06e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "97f27573837ef96b4ba42af463cc800cab615c0e <8363c02863332992a1822688da41f881d88d1631"}, {"id": "68db6d3e-a36d-3ffd-a49f-9986c9b799ec", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b569ff8a1bc1bcd4fdc6fd334604a654f61237a1 <2d2c32b1b9e32f25214f0cbc818c4d55f7da1d0e"}, {"id": "69b895de-7891-3f52-859a-7340cce08c36", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.19.4 <6.19.7"}, {"id": "e728de6d-36a0-3db2-968f-9c4d650d2f9a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2611c9616cb52d3ed54a6095d72d18e645a6955a <a6317704edab95d66a62fc1861d9546284ab678e"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9d52a97e-9253-33fb-99a1-e35acdecc885", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}